WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Barclays now sees Tesla energy storage nearly sold out for 2027 on data-centered demand. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 646. A new training cluster, the first India sales year, and cybercabs at the Austin Grand Prix come next, then counterpoint and first principles. Barclays lifted its Tesla rating from equal weight to overweight according to investing. The firm raised its price target from $370 to $450. It expects Tesla automotive revenue to return to

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:37.120
growth in 2026 after 2 years of declines. Further gains in 2027 would come from full self-driving

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.780
or FSD demand and higher exports out of Giga Shanghai. Robotaxi miles driven have accelerated

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:50.980
sharply since the June 2025 launch. FSD uptake exceeded 75% of new North American vehicles

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:57.960
in the third quarter of 2026. Barkley's also flags a potential Tesla SpaceX merger that would include

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:03.795
a premium for Tesla shareholders. Tesla plans a 20,000-rowbot artificial intelligence

00:01:03.795 --> 00:01:10.335
or AI training cluster, according to 36KR. The investment is approximately 14 billion

00:01:10.335 --> 00:01:16.155
yuan. The cluster is positioned to support expanded training runs for both FSD and Optimus.

00:01:16.635 --> 00:01:21.775
The scale is one of the largest single-announced compute commitments tied directly to Tesla's robotics

00:01:21.775 --> 00:01:27.574
and autonomy roadmap. India now has its first full year of Tesla vehicle sales on the books.

00:01:27.574 --> 00:01:29.734
ETV Barat reports.

00:01:30.194 --> 00:01:33.434
Revenue from those sales was 247 crore rupees.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:39.034
Tesla sold 650 Model Y units during the first half of fiscal 2027.

00:01:39.594 --> 00:01:43.934
The figures marked the first measurable footprint after the brand entered the market with Model

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:44.874
Y availability.

00:01:45.574 --> 00:01:50.334
Revenue and volume together give the first public snapshot of dealer and delivery operations

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:50.954
in the country.

00:01:51.923 --> 00:01:56.843
Tesla India's first-year results also cover Model Y sales and the broader vehicle revenue

00:01:56.843 --> 00:02:02.423
line according to India today. Whether early revenue translated into positive margins after

00:02:02.423 --> 00:02:07.223
import duties, logistics, and local overhead is the question those numbers now sit against.

00:02:08.405 --> 00:02:13.285
Tesla ran an expanded Robotaxi service around Circuit of the Americas during the United States

00:02:13.285 --> 00:02:20.305
Grand Prix. Tesla Roddy reports, Ashok Ellis-Swami shared a photo of a long line of gold cybercabs and

00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:26.985
Model Y Robotaxies near the track. CyberCab's spotter recorded 1,250 sightings on qualifying

00:02:26.985 --> 00:02:34.785
day, up from the prior record of 1,072. The Texas Registry listed 463 CyberCabs at mid-day

00:02:34.785 --> 00:02:41.145
Sunday. Service ran until 1am with limited drop-off zones. Riders used the expanded zone that

00:02:41.145 --> 00:02:46.485
wrapped the track toward Elroy and FM812, and the fleet handled post-race demand without

00:02:46.485 --> 00:02:48.965
a prior public announcement of the schedule change.

00:02:49.771 --> 00:02:53.611
Fremont has started producing Optimus units, tech times reports.

00:02:54.271 --> 00:02:58.071
Tesla posted a 43% drop in profit as that production began.

00:02:58.731 --> 00:03:01.091
No external buyers have been secured for the robots.

00:03:01.691 --> 00:03:06.671
The production start coincides with the profit decline, and the humanoid program is still early

00:03:06.671 --> 00:03:08.891
stage relative to current financial results.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:13.561
A Tesla Model 3 went through a five-year check, digital-today reports.

00:03:13.561 --> 00:03:20.041
parts. The pack retained 92.8% of its original battery capacity. The result is one of the longer

00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:24.901
real-world data points on degradation for the refreshed Model 3 platform under typical

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:30.723
daily use. A Dallas Fort Worth homeowner modeled a year of meter data on a free overnight

00:03:30.723 --> 00:03:36.363
electricity plan, according to Shattered. The home has a 17 kilowatt solar array and two

00:03:36.363 --> 00:03:42.943
power walls. The plan could deliver roughly $717 in annual savings. The Tesla credit pays

00:03:42.943 --> 00:03:47.583
$400 per power wall per year, but restricts how the batteries can be used.

00:03:48.003 --> 00:03:54.063
63% of current imports already occur between 9 pm and 6 am, so grid charging overnight

00:03:54.063 --> 00:03:59.743
could cut daytime imports from 4,412 kilowatt hours to about 620.

00:04:00.223 --> 00:04:04.743
There is no confirmation yet that the plan will accept that distributed generation system,

00:04:05.163 --> 00:04:08.243
or how deep daily cycling will affect six-year-old batteries.

00:04:08.243 --> 00:04:14.075
Competitors are now trying to close Tesla's lead in autonomous driving and humanoid robotics.

00:04:14.555 --> 00:04:19.955
The Financial Times reports, Tesla is advancing those AI programs while other firms work

00:04:19.955 --> 00:04:20.875
to match the pace.

00:04:21.435 --> 00:04:26.095
Training infrastructure and vehicle software are described as unmatched at scale by rivals.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:32.160
Tesla is placing its largest bet on AI and autonomous driving rather than traditional vehicle

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.620
sales, according to Meja.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:39.000
The strategy is presented as a deliberate pivot that reorders capital allocation away from

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:44.300
pure automotive volume. AI-related revenue streams are expected to surpass car margins

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:50.715
in the longer term. Ferrari CEO Benedetto Vignia praised the Tesla Roadster for both technology

00:04:50.715 --> 00:04:56.955
and presentation, HT Auto Reports. He gave it a 10 out of 10. He credited the reveal

00:04:56.955 --> 00:05:01.355
with showing the industry can still innovate and said the automotive world still has a lot

00:05:01.355 --> 00:05:06.295
to be done. The comments followed the car's demonstration at the SpaceX test facility,

00:05:06.295 --> 00:05:11.275
where it used a suction fan system and compressed gas thrusters for the inverted sequence.

00:05:12.102 --> 00:05:17.162
Franz von Holeshausen drove that same newly revealed roadster to the Peterson Museum dinner.

00:05:17.742 --> 00:05:18.662
Teslerotti reports,

00:05:19.482 --> 00:05:22.922
the arrival gave attendees a close look at the production intense styling

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:26.182
and proportions ahead of the public display inside the museum.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:32.570
Tesler is entering direct competition with VinFast in Vietnam, a T.S. Alamming post notes.

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:38.510
The match-up pits Tesla's established global supply chain and software stack against VinFast's

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:43.610
local manufacturing base and growing domestic presence. Early positioning will test pricing,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:49.797
charging access, and model range head-to-head. The Tesla app displayed full functionality on an

00:05:49.797 --> 00:05:55.497
iPhone Duo foldable device. Owners testing the dual-screen layout reported seamless access to

00:05:55.497 --> 00:06:01.297
controls, climate, and vehicle status without additional configuration. The compatibility expands

00:06:01.297 --> 00:06:04.617
the range of hardware on which the app performs without compromise.

00:06:05.717 --> 00:06:10.697
Spectacle around the roads to reveal does not address declines in Tesla's core automotive margins

00:06:10.697 --> 00:06:17.717
and slowing growth. 36KR argues. The analysis questions whether new programs can offset those trends

00:06:17.717 --> 00:06:23.497
without clearer volume recovery. It treats the event as a distraction rather than a fix for the company's

00:06:23.497 --> 00:06:28.797
primary business lines. The visual impact of the upside-down demonstration is set against the

00:06:28.797 --> 00:06:33.477
need for sustained delivery growth and margin expansion in the existing vehicle portfolio.

00:06:34.157 --> 00:06:38.937
Investor attention may remain split until automotive fundamentals show measurable improvement

00:06:38.937 --> 00:06:40.297
beyond one-time events.

00:06:41.355 --> 00:06:45.635
Energy storage is the other engine, and it is now the physical layer those training runs

00:06:45.635 --> 00:06:46.115
sit on.

00:06:46.735 --> 00:06:49.375
Potential shipment growth sits above 50%.

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:54.335
That book gives the energy group multi-year revenue visibility the automotive segment has

00:06:54.335 --> 00:06:55.475
lacked in recent years.

00:06:55.475 --> 00:06:58.455
The economics are not the same as vehicle margins.

00:06:59.095 --> 00:07:04.095
Spend on the training cluster has to come back through higher value AI services, not through

00:07:04.095 --> 00:07:04.775
car deliveries.

00:07:05.475 --> 00:07:09.155
Storage also runs on a different supply chain than the vehicle platforms.

00:07:09.775 --> 00:07:14.015
Battery cells, inverters, and site integration each move on their own clocks.

00:07:14.495 --> 00:07:19.095
When data center buyers crowd out other customers, Tesla gets more pricing power.

00:07:19.535 --> 00:07:23.935
It also has to choose who gets the hardware, a decision that was not on the table when this

00:07:23.935 --> 00:07:29.815
business was mostly residential. The cluster's capital intensity only works if storage margins stay

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:35.095
stable enough to keep funding compute. If the energy side can take the output of new cell lines

00:07:35.095 --> 00:07:40.815
and throw off steadier cash than automotive, the argument for more AI compute spend gets stronger.

00:07:41.415 --> 00:07:46.015
Factories that once chased vehicle volume now feed storage customers who pay for uptime,

00:07:46.495 --> 00:07:52.395
not for range or acceleration. The margin shape is narrower and more durable if Tesla executes

00:07:52.395 --> 00:07:57.195
on grid scale projects. That is a different test than hitting a quarterly delivery number.

00:07:57.875 --> 00:08:02.655
How Tesla splits output between data center megapacks and residential power walls will decide

00:08:02.655 --> 00:08:08.608
how fast energy can grow without stretching cell supply. Before we go, tomorrow's question is

00:08:08.608 --> 00:08:13.048
whether that Texas free nights plan actually accepts a home solar and power wall setup,

00:08:13.488 --> 00:08:17.628
like the one that was modeled. And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

